    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-14T15:56:02+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-14T15:56:02+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T06:26:02Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-14T06:26:02Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred in the Bight, is slowly drifting to the southeast to be located west of Tasmania on Saturday and in the Tasman Sea on Monday. A ridge of high pressure is expected to remain over South Australia. A trough over QLD pushes into the far northeast of SA from later Saturday through to later Monday. A trough of low pressure moves in the far west of South Australia later on Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-14T15:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T05:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Winds southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Yunta, most likely in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 23.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:00am to 2:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely at night. Winds southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Leigh Creek, medium chance elsewhere. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 27.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
